---
import RolePage from '../../components/pages/RolePage.astro';
import InvoicingHighlight from '../../components/sections/InvoicingHighlight.astro';
---

<RolePage
  lang="en"
  title="For treasurers — Rondo"
  description="Rondo for treasurers: dues rules, invoicing, payment status and dashboard in one workflow."
  kicker="For your role"
  roleTitle="Treasurer"
  intro="Work from one financial workflow: dues rules, bulk invoicing, automatic follow-up and a dashboard showing what needs attention now."
  demoLabel="Look at the demo"
  contactLabel="Contact us"
  contactHref="/en/contact"
  screenshotSrc="/screenshot-finance-dashboard.webp"
  screenshotAlt="Finance dashboard in Rondo Club"
  screenshotWidth={1600}
  screenshotHeight={900}
  whatHeading="What this solves"
  bulletPoints={[
    'Dues rules with family discounts and pro-rata without separate calculations.',
    'Bulk invoicing and automatic reminders from the same system.',
    'Immediate insight into outstanding amounts, recent payments and follow-up actions.',
  ]}
  cards={[
    { title: 'From rule to invoice', text: 'You configure rules per team or category; Rondo generates the right invoices.' },
    { title: 'Automatic status updates', text: 'Payment status updates after payment, including history per invoice.' },
    { title: 'More control, fewer ad-hoc checks', text: 'The dashboard helps prioritize what needs immediate follow-up.' },
  ]}
  otherHeading="Other paths"
  otherPrefix="Also relevant:"
  otherAnd="and"
  hasExtra={true}
  otherLinks={[
    { href: '/en/for-secretary', label: 'For secretaries' },
    { href: '/en/for-gate-volunteer', label: 'For access & events' },
  ]}
>
  <InvoicingHighlight lang="en" />

  <div class="finance-overview-block">
    <h2 class="gradient-text finance-overview-heading">Finance dashboard and unbilled overview</h2>

    <div class="finance-overview-copy">
      <p>
        The finance dashboard shows what matters right now: outstanding amount, recent payments, and actions that need
        follow-up.
      </p>
      <p>
        In the <em>Still to invoice</em> overview, you can see exactly which members are not yet part of an invoice
        run. This helps you avoid missed invoices and keep billing predictable throughout the season.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="finance-overview-grid">
      <figure class="finance-overview-shot">
        <img
          class="zoomable-screenshot"
          src="/Screenshots/financien-dashboard.png"
          alt="Finance dashboard with outstanding amount, recent payments and actions"
          width="3456"
          height="1922"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="finance-overview-shot">
        <img
          class="zoomable-screenshot"
          src="/Screenshots/contributie-nog-te-factureren.png"
          alt="Overview of members that are still to be invoiced"
          width="3456"
          height="1922"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="finance-installments-block">
    <h2 class="gradient-text finance-installments-heading">Instalment payments without high extra costs</h2>

    <div class="finance-installments-copy">
      <p>
        Not every member pays dues in one go. With Rondo, you offer a personal payment page where members can choose
        to pay in 3 or 8 instalments.
        If fewer instalments are still possible in the season, Rondo automatically adjusts the available options.
      </p>
      <p>
        That choice runs automatically in the same invoice workflow, without high additional costs for either club or
        member. Transaction fees can be configured separately per invoice type.
        This keeps dues accessible while the treasurer stays in control.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="finance-shots-grid">
      <figure class="finance-shot finance-shot-portrait">
        <img
          class="zoomable-screenshot"
          src="/Screenshots/screenshot-payment-page.png"
          alt="Personal payment page with instalment payment options"
          width="1058"
          height="1866"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
      <figure class="finance-shot">
        <img
          class="zoomable-screenshot"
          src="/Screenshots/screenshot-invoice.png"
          alt="Invoice detail in Rondo Club"
          width="1686"
          height="2278"
          loading="lazy"
        />
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>

  <figure class="treasurer-quote">
    <blockquote>
      "At AWC, we see every day how much pressure volunteers are under. With Rondo, we finally have a platform that
      truly takes work off our hands. Member administration, dues collection and financial alignment now run in one
      integrated, clear flow. It saves us hours of work and gives us the insights to steer the club better. That
      makes my role as treasurer both more enjoyable and more effective."
    </blockquote>
    <figcaption class="treasurer-quote-author">
      <img src="/xander-notte.webp" alt="Xander Notte" width="400" height="400" loading="lazy" />
      <div>
        <p class="treasurer-quote-name">Xander Notte</p>
        <p class="treasurer-quote-role">Treasurer at AWC</p>
      </div>
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</RolePage>

<style>
  .finance-overview-block {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 2rem auto 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .finance-overview-block {
      grid-template-columns: 0.95fr 1.05fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .finance-overview-heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.1rem);
    margin: 0;
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .finance-overview-copy p {
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
  }

  .finance-overview-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .finance-overview-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .finance-overview-shot {
    border-radius: 1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(0, 27, 96, 0.16);
    border: 1px solid #D8E3EE;
    background: #FFFFFF;
  }

  .finance-overview-shot img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .finance-installments-block {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 2rem auto 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 980px) {
    .finance-installments-block {
      grid-template-columns: 0.85fr 1.15fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .finance-installments-heading {
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2.1rem);
    margin: 0;
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
  }

  .finance-installments-copy p {
    color: #475569;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
  }

  .finance-shots-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.85rem;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  @media (min-width: 700px) {
    .finance-shots-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 0.50fr 1.0fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .finance-shot {
    border-radius: 1rem;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 18px 45px rgba(0, 27, 96, 0.16);
    border: 1px solid #D8E3EE;
    background: #FFFFFF;
  }

  .finance-shot img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  .finance-shot-portrait img {
    max-height: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: #F8FAFC;
  }

  .treasurer-quote {
    max-width: 72rem;
    margin: 1.75rem auto 0;
    padding: 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid #D8E3EE;
    background: #FFFFFF;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0, 27, 96, 0.08);
  }

  .treasurer-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #334155;
  }

  .treasurer-quote-author {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.8rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  .treasurer-quote-author img {
    width: 3rem;
    height: 3rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .treasurer-quote-name {
    margin: 0;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #0F172A;
  }

  .treasurer-quote-role {
    margin: 0;
    color: #64748B;
  }
</style>
